AB  - Intensive grassland management or the use of herbicides can reduce weeds but environment protection requirements often prohibit these measures. The preservation of extensive grassland has great conservation value. In order to combine economic and ecological interests on these areas, site-specific and non-chemical solutions are necessary. A suitable weed control device and an effective management strategy were developed for this purpose. First, images of the field were acquired with a drone. Then, an image analysis using a neural network detected individual weeds. This led to an application map for a robot-or tractor-mounted treatment tool. This was done for the example of the poisonous weed Colchicum autumnale. This paper focuses on the developed tractor-mounted implement. The working width was divided into individually controllable sections. Each section had a high-pressure water jet which was only activated over detected weeds. © 2022, VDI Verlag GMBH. All rights reserved.
